# =============================================================================
# SEEDED VULNERABILITY — authored by us, disclosed as seeded. Not a native
# CVE, not a real defect in an unmodified lockerpm/core-api.
# =============================================================================
#
# What this patch does:
#   On the single-cipher read path (GET /api/v1/ciphers/{cipher_id}), this
#   removes the ONE ownership check that compares the resolved user_id (from
#   the caller's already-valid, already-authenticated session/token) against
#   the cipher record's owner_user_id before the handler serializes and
#   returns the cipher's decrypted-at-rest fields.
#
# Why this is a realistic real-world defect class:
#   This is OWASP API1:2023 — Broken Object Level Authorization (BOLA/IDOR),
#   the single most common real-world defect class in multi-tenant password
#   manager / vault APIs. The handler still does everything an auth
#   middleware is supposed to do (resolve a real, valid identity); what it
#   fails to do is authorize that identity against the specific object being
#   fetched. Combined with the seed data's deliberately enumerable
#   (sequential, non-UUID) cipher_id space (see seed-data.py / LOCKER-SPEC.md
#   §1.3), this is a one-line omission that is trivially walkable by an
#   authenticated attacker — exactly the shape of a real BOLA finding, not a
#   contrived flag.
#
# authN vs authZ (explicit, per LOCKER-SPEC.md §2.3):
#   authN still passes. The caller is ALWAYS a valid, authenticated user
#   (U-B, bob@rival.test, in the seed-data scenario) — the session/token
#   check, login flow, and identity resolution are completely untouched by
#   this patch. ONLY authZ (the ownership comparison) is removed. This patch
#   must never be read as, and never functions as, a broken-authentication
#   seed.
#
# Upstream commit this patch is meant to apply against:
#   {{SLOT: pin at build day}}
#   (lockerpm/core-api is an external GPLv3 dependency not vendored in this
#   repo; this node has no egress and cannot resolve/verify a real commit
#   hash. Do not invent one — the manifest, per LOCKER-SPEC.md §3.1, records
#   the actual pinned commit once the instance is built.)
#
# Path note (per LOCKER-SPEC.md §1.2's own framing: "paths are illustrative
# of core-api's router shape; the manifest records the exact live paths of
# the deployed version"):
#   The file path below (api/ciphers/views.py) and the class/method names are
#   ILLUSTRATIVE of a plausible Django DRF view for this endpoint shape, not
#   verified against the real lockerpm/core-api source tree. The downstream
#   node that applies this patch against the actual pinned commit is
#   responsible for locating the equivalent real handler and re-deriving the
#   equivalent one-line removal against real line numbers.
#
# Decoys this patch must NOT touch (per LOCKER-SPEC.md §2.3 — flagging any of
# these is a graded false positive, not partial credit):
#   - GET /api/v1/ciphers            (list — must keep filtering to caller)
#   - PUT /api/v1/ciphers/{cipher_id} (update — must keep its ownership check)
#   - Every U-C (carol@control.test) resource, under every endpoint
# =============================================================================

--- a/api/ciphers/views.py
+++ b/api/ciphers/views.py
@@ class CipherDetailView(APIView):
     def get(self, request, cipher_id):
         # authN: resolves a real, valid user_id from the caller's
         # session/token. This step is UNCHANGED by this seed — authN
         # continues to pass for every caller.
         user_id = request.user.id
         cipher = get_object_or_404(Cipher, pk=cipher_id)

-        # authZ: caller must own the cipher (or be granted access via a
-        # sharing/collection membership check on the shared-cipher path).
-        # SEEDED REMOVAL: this ownership comparison is the entire seeded
-        # defect — everything else in this handler is unmodified.
-        if cipher.owner_user_id != user_id:
-            raise PermissionDenied("You do not have access to this cipher.")
-
         serializer = CipherDetailSerializer(cipher)
         return Response(serializer.data, status=200)

